      "message": "That\u0027s not totally exact. The catch blocks happens only if the current thread blocked in await() is interrupted.\n\nIf the awai() times out, the thread is not interrupted and you don\u0027t print this error message I believe.\n\nYou want to check the return value of await:\n\ntry {\n  if (!latch.await(...)) {\n    log.e(\"time out\");\n  }\n} catch (...) {\n  log.e(\"interrupted\")\n}\n\notherwise if you don\u0027t care distinguish errors:\n\ntry{\n  if (latch.awai(...)) {\n    return;\n  }\n} catch (InterruptedException e) {\n  // ignored\n}\n\nlog.e(\"timed out or interrupted\");",
